   "text": "I read the drawing as a DOTA-type chelator joined through a lysine to a piperazine-linked FAP-targeting quinoline unit and a 4-iodophenylbutanoyl albumin-binder arm.\n\n- **Chelator:** a cyclen ring (four N, four CH2CH2 bridges). Three nitrogens carry CH2COOH. The fourth carries CH2C(=O)NH\u2013, which links to the lysine side chain.\n- **Lysine:** the \u03b5-NH is acylated by the chelator and the \u03b1-carbon is (S). The \u03b1-NH carries a glutaryl linker, and the carboxyl end is an amide to the piperazine nitrogen.\n- **Piperazine arm:** the other piperazine nitrogen carries \u2013(CH2)3\u2013O\u2013 attached at the 6-position of a quinoline. The quinoline 4-position bears C(=O)NH\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013 on a pyrrolidine nitrogen. That pyrrolidine has 4,4-difluoro and a 2-cyano group with (S) configuration.\n- **Albumin-binder arm:** the glutaryl linker ends in an amide to the \u03b1-amino group of a second lysine, whose COOH is free. Its \u03b5-NH is acylated by 4-(4-iodophenyl)butanoyl.\n\nTwo readings are assumed rather than certain. The glutaryl linker is taken as five carbons (C(=O)CH2CH2CH2C(=O)), and each lysine chain as four CH2 groups. The second lysine \u03b1-carbon is drawn with plain bonds, so it carries no stereo label.\n\nI checked both (S) centres by working out the CIP priorities from the drawing and matching them to the chirality tags in the SMILES; both come out as `[C@H]`.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCC(=O)NC(C(=O)O)CCCCNC(=O)CCCc2ccc(I)cc2)C(=O)N2CCN(CCCOc3ccc4nccc(C(=O)NCC(=O)N5CC(F)(F)C[C@H]5C#N)c4c3)CC2)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CC1"
